visit_ExceptHandler iterates `for statement in node.body` and only pattern-matches Return/Raise/Expr at that top level. Any exit-0 nested one level deeper is invisible.

Reproduced -- reported clean, exit 0:

    def sweep(items):
        failures = []
        for item in items:
            try:
                run(item)
            except HardError as error:
                failures.append(error)
            except TransientError as e:
                if is_transient(e):
                    return 0
        return 1 if failures else 0

A conditional swallow inside the handler is arguably the most common form of this bug in practice (classify the error, then decide to swallow), so this is a large hole in an otherwise-cheap check.
